  "promptEn": "Blues in Bb. Which scale sounds in the fragment?",
  "explanationEs": "La respuesta correcta es «Escala de blues». En Si♭ la escala de blues es Si♭, Re♭, Mi♭, Mi natural, Fa, La♭ y Si♭. La quinta disminuida es Mi natural, entre Mi♭ y Fa; la tercera menor es Re♭ y la séptima menor es La♭. La armadura de Si♭ mayor ya incluye Si♭ y Mi♭, así que la escala se lee con alteraciones pocas veces.",
  "explanationEn": "The correct answer is “Blues scale”. In Bb the blues scale is Bb, Db, Eb, E, F, Ab and Bb. The diminished fifth is E natural, between Eb and F; the minor third is Db and the minor seventh is Ab. The Bb major key signature already includes Bb and Eb, so the scale is read with few accidentals.",
